cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  pydreg is an inference-only port of dREG (Danko Lab) -- please also
  cite the original dREG papers listed under `references` below (and in
  the README's "Citation" section) to credit the underlying method.
type: software
title: pydreg
version: 0.3.1
date-released: '2026-08-23'
abstract: >-
  An inference-only Python port of dREG (Danko Lab) for detecting active
  transcriptional regulatory elements (promoters and enhancers) from
  PRO-seq/GRO-seq nascent-transcription data.
authors:
  - given-names: Adam Youlin
    family-names: He
    email: adamyhe@gmail.com
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/adamyhe/pydreg
url: https://github.com/adamyhe/pydreg
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - bigwig
  - genomics
  - transcriptional regulation
  - pro-seq
  - gro-seq
  - peak calling
  - svm
